Angel food cake","dish/angel-food-cake"],["Applebee's","dish/applebee-s"],["Arby's","dish/arby-s"],["Arnold's Bar and Grill","dish/arnold-s-bar-and-grill"],["Banana bread","dish/banana-bread"],["Banana pudding","dish/banana-pudding"],["Barbecue sauce","dish/barbecue-sauce"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beer cake","dish/beer-cake"],["Ben's Chili Bowl","dish/ben-s-chili-bowl"],["Benjy's","dish/benjy-s"],["Besaw's","dish/besaw-s"],["Better than sex cake","dish/better-than-sex-cake"],["Blackhawk (restaurant)","dish/blackhawk-restaurant"],["Blini","dish/blini"],["Blooming onion","dish/blooming-onion"],["Bobcat Bite","dish/bobcat-bite"],["Boiling Springs Tavern","dish/boiling-springs-tavern"],["Brix Tavern","dish/brix-tavern"],["Brown Betty (dessert)","dish/brown-betty-dessert"],["Brown Derby","dish/brown-derby"],["Brunswick stew","dish/brunswick-stew"],["Buffalo wing","dish/buffalo-wing"],["Buona","dish/buona"],["Busboys and Poets","dish/busboys-and-poets"],["Butter cake","dish/butter-cake"],["Byways Cafe","dish/byways-cafe"],["Caesar salad","dish/caesar-salad"],["California Grill","dish/california-grill"],["Camp Washington Chili","dish/camp-washington-chili"],["Caramel apple","dish/caramel-apple"],["Carbonara","dish/carbonara"],["Carnation Cafe","dish/carnation-cafe"],["Cheesesteak","dish/cheesesteak"],["Chicago-style hot dog","dish/chicago-style-hot-dog"],["Chicken nugget","dish/chicken-nugget"],["Chiffon cake","dish/chiffon-cake"],["Chili con carne","dish/chili-con-carne"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/6/63/Southeast_Portland%2C_Oregon_%28January_2021%29_124.jpg/500px-Southeast_Portland%2C_Oregon_%28January_2021%29_124.jpg","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Another Believer","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Southeast_Portland%2C_Oregon_(January_2021)_124.jpg"}},"ingredient/tartaric-acid":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/tartaric-acid","n":"Tartaric acid","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 2 dishes across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Tartaric acid is a white, crystalline organic acid that occurs naturally in many fruits, most notably in grapes but also in tamarinds, bananas, avocados,  and citrus. Its salt, potassium bitartrate, commonly known as cream of tartar, develops naturally in the process of fermentation. Potassium bitartrate is commonly mixed with sodium bicarbonate and is sold as baking powder used as a leavening agent in food preparation. The acid itself is added to foods as an antioxidant E334 and to impart its distinctive sour taste. Naturally occurring tartaric acid is a useful raw material in organic synthesis. Tartaric acid, an alpha-hydroxy-carboxylic acid, is diprotic and aldaric in acid characteristics and is a dihydroxyl derivative of succinic acid."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-tartaric-acid"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tartaric_acid"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["British cuisine","cuisine/british-cuisine",[["Digestive biscuit","dish/digestive-biscuit"],["Jammie Dodgers","dish/jammie-dodgers"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Malic acid","ingredient/malic-acid"],["Sodium bicarbonate","ingredient/sodium-bicarbonate"],["Sugar","ingredient/sugar"],["Wheat flour","ingredient/wheat-flour"],["Butter","ingredient/butter"],["Leavening agent","ingredient/leavening-agent"],["Malt extract","ingredient/malt-extract"],["Wholemeal","ingredient/wholemeal"],["Apples","ingredient/apples"],["Raspberries","ingredient/raspberries"],["Raspberry jam","ingredient/raspberry-jam"],["Shortbread","ingredient/shortbread"],["Strawberries","ingredient/strawberries"]]}]},"ingredient/domestic-goose":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/domestic-goose","n":"Domestic goose","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 2 cuisines","intro":[["A domestic goose is a goose that humans have domesticated and kept for their meat, eggs, or down feathers, or as companion animals. Domestic geese have been derived through selective breeding from the wild greylag goose (Anser anser domesticus) and swan goose (Anser cygnoides domesticus)."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-domestic-goose"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Domestic_goose"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":2,"groups":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine",[["Foie gras","dish/foie-gras"]]],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine",[["Foie gras","dish/foie-gras"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Domestic duck","ingredient/domestic-duck"],["Liver","ingredient/liver"],["Liver as food","ingredient/liver-as-food"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/2/27/Sunset_Park_-_Las_Vegas_%2811044584144%29.jpg/500px-Sunset_Park_-_Las_Vegas_%2811044584144%29.jpg","w":500,"h":366,"by":"Tomás Del Coro from Las Vegas, Nevada, USA","lic":"CC BY-SA 2.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/2.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sunset_Park_-_Las_Vegas_(11044584144).jpg"}},"dish/kadowaki-restaurant":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/kadowaki-restaurant","n":"Kadowaki (restaurant)","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Japanese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Azabu Kadowaki, or Kadowaki for short, is a Michelin 3-star Kaiseki restaurant in Azabu-Jūban, Japan run by chef Toshima Kadowaki. The restaurant opened in August 2000 and initially refused Michelin stars, before gaining two stars in 2010 and subsequently gained 3 stars in 2020."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kadowaki-restaurant"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kadowaki_(restaurant)"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Japanese cuisine","cuisine/japanese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Just One Cookboo