rant on Seattle's Capitol Hill, in the US state of Washington."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-kedai-makan"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kedai_Makan"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Malaysian cuisine","cuisine/malaysian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Rasa Malaysia","ref":"site/rasamalaysia-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"rasamalaysia.com","note":"Penang-born Bee Yinn Low's recipe site, including Malaysian and Nyonya dishes.","url":"https://rasamalaysia.com/nyonya-recipes/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Malaysian cuisine","links":[["Nasi goreng","dish/nasi-goreng"],["Thali","dish/thali"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/1/10/Kedai_Makan%2C_Seattle_%282023%29_-_2.jpg/500px-Kedai_Makan%2C_Seattle_%282023%29_-_2.jpg","w":500,"h":667,"by":"Another Believer","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kedai_Makan%2C_Seattle_(2023)_-_2.jpg"}},"ingredient/lamian":{"t":"ingredient","r":"ingredient/lamian","n":"Lamian","c":"#c9b8dd","crumb":[["Ingredients","ingredients"]],"sub":"Ingredient in 1 dish across 1 cuisine","intro":[["Lamian is a type of soft wheat flour handmade Chinese noodle that is particularly common in northern China. Lamian is made by twisting, stretching and folding the dough into strands, using the weight of the dough. The length and thickness of the strands depends on the number of times the dough is folded."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"ingredient-lamian"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lamian"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's cooked with","count":1,"groups":[["Chinese cuisine","cuisine/chinese-cuisine",[["Lanzhou beef noodles","dish/lanzhou-beef-noodles"]]]]},{"h":"Often cooked with","links":[["Beef","ingredient/beef"],["Beef broth","ingredient/beef-broth"],["Chinese noodles","ingredient/chinese-noodles"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/0/0c/%E5%85%B0%E5%B7%9E%E7%89%9B%E8%82%89%E9%9D%A2.jpg/500px-%E5%85%B0%E5%B7%9E%E7%89%9B%E8%82%89%E9%9D%A2.jpg","w":500,"h":333,"by":"三猎","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%E5%85%B0%E5%B7%9E%E7%89%9B%E8%82%89%E9%9D%A2.jpg"}},"dish/mohinga":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/mohinga","n":"Mohinga","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Burmese cuisine","dot":"#f0b340","intro":[["Mohinga is the national dish of Myanmar. Mohinga is a fish soup made with rice noodles, typically served as a hearty breakfast. It features a rich broth flavored with lemongrass, turmeric, and fish sauce, often garnished with boiled eggs, cilantro, and crispy fritters. Mohinga is readily available in most parts of the country, sold by street hawkers and roadside stalls in larger cities. Mohinga is traditionally eaten for breakfast, but nowadays it is eaten at any time of day. Egg, onions, or parsley can be added to the dish.Monhinga being named a the Belt and Road International Day food."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-mohinga"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mohinga"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Burmese cuisine","cuisine/burmese-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Rice vermicelli","ingredient/rice-vermicelli"]]},{"h":"More from Burmese cuisine","links":[["Burmese salads","dish/burmese-salads"],["Khao soi","dish/khao-soi"],["Thali","dish/thali"],["Thua nao","dish/thua-nao"],["Top Burmese","dish/top-burmese"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/4/4e/IMG_Mohinga.JPG/500px-IMG_Mohinga.JPG","w":500,"h":375,"by":"Wagaung","lic":"CC BY-SA 3.0","licUrl":"http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:IMG_Mohinga.JPG"}},"dish/ofada-rice":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/ofada-rice","n":"Ofada rice","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish from Nigerian cuisine","dot":"#e46a3f","intro":[["Ofada rice is a Yoruba Nigerian dish. It is the name of an indigenous rice from a small community called Ofada, located in the Obafemi Owode Local Government Area of Ogun State. It is not exclusively grown in the community, but it is an indigenous rice grown in southwest Nigeria which is named after the Ofada community. It is used in making a variety of dishes. Ofada rice are mostly blends, and some of the rice varieties in the blends are not indigenous to Africa; however, they usually also contain African rice. It is grown almost exclusively in Ogun State, a state in southwestern Nigeria. Ofada rice is grown on free-draining soil where the water table is permanently below the root of the plant."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-ofada-rice"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ofada_rice"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["Nigerian cuisine","cuisine/nigerian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Ingredients","count":1,"links":[["Iru","ingredient/iru"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Kitchen Butterfly","ref":"site/kitchenbutterfly-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"kitchenbutterfly.com","note":"Long-running blog by Nigerian food writer and historian Ozoz Sokoh, with Nigerian and New Nigerian recipes.","url":"https://www.kitchenbutterfly.com/about-2","suggested":true},{"name":"Sisi Yemmie","ref":"site/sisiyemmie-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"sisiyemmie.com","note":"Nigerian home cooking recipes and meal plans, paired with the SisiYemmieTV YouTube channel.","url":"https://sisiyemmie.com/","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from Nigerian cuisine","links":[["Akadi","dish/akadi"],["Edikang ikong","dish/edikang-ikong"],["Edo black soup","dish/edo-black-soup"],["Miyar zogale","dish/miyar-zogale"],["Moin moin","dish/moin-moin"],["Palm nut soup","dish/palm-nut-soup"],["Sinasir","dish/sinasir"],["Suya","dish/suya"]]}],"img":{"src":"/labs/cuisines/img/thumb/8/85/Ofada_Rice.jpg/500px-Ofada_Rice.jpg","w":500,"h":521,"by":"Ijeoma","lic":"CC BY-SA 4.0","licUrl":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/4.0","page":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ofada_Rice.jpg"}},"dish/robuchon-au-dome":{"t":"dish","r":"dish/robuchon-au-dome","n":"Robuchon au Dôme","c":"#ede6da","crumb":[["Dishes","dishes"]],"sub":"Dish found in 2 cuisines","dot":"#cf5f87","intro":[["Robuchon au Dôme is a three Michelin-star restaurant in Macau and is part of the L'Atelier de Joël Robuchon gourmet restaurant chain. The restaurant was established originally in 2001 at the Lisboa Hotel under the name Robuchon á Galera before being moved in 2011 to its current location inside the glass dome at the top of the Grand Lisboa hotel on the 43rd floor. The restaurant is run by French chef Julien Tongourian who is also the executive chef of L'Atelier's Hong Kong location who had worked with Joel Robuchon for over 25 years. The restaurant was awarded 3 Michelin stars in 2009 and has maintained all its stars since then."]],"src":"wikipedia","actions":[{"kind":"globe","hash":"dish-robuchon-au-dome"},{"kind":"wiki","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robuchon_au_D%C3%B4me"}],"sections":[{"h":"Where it's from","links":[["French cuisine","cuisine/french-cuisine"],["New Caledonian cuisine","cuisine/new-caledonian-cuisine"]]},{"h":"Cook it","rows":[{"name":"Pardon Your French","ref":"site/pardonyourfrench-com","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"pardonyourfrench.com","note":"Audrey Le Goff, a French cook, shares classic and regional French home recipes.","url":"https://pardonyourfrench.com","suggested":true},{"name":"La Cuisine de Géraldine","ref":"site/lacuisinedegeraldine-fr","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"lacuisinedegeraldine.fr","note":"French home cooking blog by Géraldine Leverd, also author of The New French Kitchen.","url":"https://lacuisinedegeraldine.fr/en/about-us","suggested":true},{"name":"New Caledonia Tourism: Kanak cooking","ref":"site/newcaledonia-travel","color":"#55b8ad","shape":"site","sub":"newcaledonia.travel","note":"Official tourism board overview of Kanak food, including bougna cooked in an earth oven.","url":"https://www.newcaledonia.travel/nz/gastronomy-wine/gastronomy/kanak-cooking","suggested":true}]},{"h":"More from French cuisine","links":[["'t Fornuis","dish/t-fornuis"],["'t Misverstant","dish/t-misverstant"],["'t Vlasbloemeken","dish/t-vlasbloemeken"],["&moshik","dish/moshik"],["Aan de Poel","dish/aan-de-poel"],["Adrian (restaurant)","dish/adrian-restaurant"],["Adventureland Bazaar","dish/adventureland-bazaar"],["Alain Ducasse at The Dorchester","dish/alain-ducasse-at-the-dorchester"],["Albufera sauce","dish/albufera-sauce"],["Alex (restaurant)","dish/alex-restaurant"],["Andouillette","dish/andouillette"],["Arpège (restaurant)","dish/arpege-restaurant"],["Aspic","dish/aspic"],["Atelier Crenn","dish/atelier-crenn"],["Au Coin des Bons Enfants","dish/au-coin-des-bons-enfants"],["Au Crocodile","dish/au-crocodile"],["Au Pied de Cochon (Mexico City)","dish/au-pied-de-cochon-mexico-city"],["Auberge (restaurant)","dish/auberge-restaurant"],["Auberge De Kieviet","dish/auberge-de-kieviet"],["Aubergine (London restaurant)","dish/aubergine-london-restaurant"],["Auguste (restaurant)","dish/auguste-restaurant"],["Bagatelle (restaurant)","dish/bagatelle-restaurant"],["Balthazar (restaurant)","dish/balthazar-restaurant"],["Bardot Brasserie","dish/bardot-brasserie"],["Bâtard (restaurant)","dish/batard-restaurant"],["Baumé (restaurant)","dish/baume-restaurant"],["Bayonne ham","dish/bayonne-ham"],["Be Our Guest Restaurant","dish/be-our-guest-restaurant"],["Beaulieu, Doorwerth Castle","dish/beaulieu-doorwerth-castle"],["Beef Stroganoff","dish/beef-stroganoff"],["Bell's (restaurant)","dish/bell-s-restaurant"],["Belmond Le Manoir aux Quat'Saisons","dish/belmond-le-manoir-aux-quat-saisons"],["Beluga (restaurant)","dish/beluga-restaurant"],["Berowra Waters Inn","dish/berowra-waters-inn"],["Beurre maître d'hô